commit 91dc1b2f3977083de570eeb277d309681dcafcfe
Author: wave7-agent <agent@rickylabs.dev>
Date:   Fri Sep 4 15:21:40 2026 +0200

    Design: a null footer column renders in the absent tone
    
    `FooterColumns` renders the em dash for a `null` value, but the tone is carried
    by `data-direction`, and a `null` value with no explicit direction emitted
    `inherit`, which no stylesheet rule matches — so the em dash painted in the
    full-contrast foreground and read as a value rather than as "not recorded".
    The gallery ships exactly that case: the Wire column.
    
    Absence now wins over a caller-supplied direction, because once the value is
    null there is no amount for a direction to qualify.

