commit 433caf984ab830af87f1defeac79669d2759352d
Author: wave7-agent <agent@rickylabs.dev>
Date:   Fri Sep 4 15:21:33 2026 +0200

    Design: clip the area chart's hover bands to the frame
    
    The chart renders correctly, but its hover layer was measured wrong at the two
    ends. Each band was centred on its point with `translateX(-50%)` and given a
    full step of width, so the first and last bands hung outside the frame by half
    a step: on the gallery's four-point chart that is ~14% of the frame's width,
    which is enough that hovering the y-axis gutter pops the first readout.
    
    An end band cannot simply be clipped, though — the crosshair, the dot and the
    tooltip all sit at `50%` of their band, so clipping would draw them off the
    point they name. The band now reports the point's x back out as `--hit-x`, a
    percentage of its own box: 50% for every interior band, and off-centre only
    where an end band was clipped. Tiling is unaffected because adjacent bands
    still meet exactly at the midpoint between their points.
    
    Verified by rendering: four points give the bands 0–17.92, 17.92–50, 50–82.08
    and 82.08–100, with every marker landing on its own x-tick (1.875, 33.958,
    66.042, 98.125).

