Fix: a null footer column renders in the absent tone

FooterColumns renders the em dash for a `null` value, but the tone is carried by
`data-direction`, and a `null` value with no explicit direction emitted
`inherit`, which no stylesheet rule matches — so the em dash painted in the
full-contrast foreground and read as a value rather than as "not recorded".

The gallery ships exactly that case: the Wire column of the second
footer-columns demo.

Absence now wins over a caller-supplied direction, because once the value is
null there is no amount for a direction to qualify. Verified by rendering:
`{ value: null }` and `{ value: null, direction: 'in' }` both emit
`data-direction="absent"`, while a measured value keeps its own direction.
EOF
