Fix: drop the hero size variant that could not change the size

`WidgetCard.Hero` took a `size` prop, and its `--lg` rule set
`--ns-text-4xl` — exactly the value the base `.ns-widget__hero .ns-money-text`
rule already sets. So `lg` changed nothing but a padding-block-start, no call
site ever passed it, and `4xl` is the largest type token in `tokens.css`, so
there was no step for it to step to.

A variant whose name promises a size and whose stylesheet cannot deliver one is
worse than no variant: the next caller would read the prop, pass `'lg'`, and
get the default back. Removed, with a note at the band recording that a bigger
page-level hero needs a display-size token first — a token-layer decision, not
a modifier on this band.

The base hero is unchanged and still renders at 4xl; verified by rendering a
composed card: hero band present, amount at `$4,158,250.50` with the currency
as its own prefixed element, delta chip on the same baseline.
EOF
