## Dead API — `WidgetCard.Hero`'s `size` prop could not change the size

**Found 2026-09-04 (design steer #2, pass 8).** `WidgetCard.Hero` accepted
`size?: 'md' | 'lg'`, and `--lg`'s rule set `font-size: var(--ns-text-4xl)` —
the same value the base `.ns-widget__hero .ns-money-text` rule already sets. No
call site ever passed it. `--ns-text-4xl` (2.25rem) is the largest type token in
`tokens.css`, so there was no step for `lg` to step to; its only distinct effect
was a `padding-block-start`.

Removed (`0d8fe41`) rather than left in place, because a variant whose name
promises a size and whose stylesheet cannot deliver one is worse than no variant
— the next caller reads the prop, passes `'lg'`, and silently gets the default.
A page-level hero that outranks every other number is still wanted (the vision
critique §5 asks for exactly it); it needs a display-size token added at the
token layer first, and `tokens.json` is the source for that, not this band.
